pve-csi-copy (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix unreachable endpoint: move the copy method from
    PVE::API2::Storage::Content ('{volume}/copy') to PVE::API2::Storage::Status
    ('{storage}/csi-copy'). The content subtree is mounted with a
    fragment-joining, greedy '{volume}' path parameter, so PVE's router fed the
    whole 'content/<vol>/copy' suffix to the BUILT-IN root-only 'copy' method as
    volume='<vol>/copy' — observed on PVE 9.2.3 as a 400 "duplicate parameter
    (already defined in URI) with conflicting values!" (or a root@pam permission
    error without a body volume). The endpoint is now
    POST /nodes/{node}/storage/{storage}/csi-copy with the source volume as a
    body parameter; handler and permissions are unchanged.
  * Harden the target volume name: apply the same strict allow-list the source
    volume already uses (reject ':', '/', '..') instead of relying on the
    destination plugin's parse_volname to reject traversal on import, so the
    endpoint's safety no longer depends on a check in a separate code path.
  * pve-csi-copy-verify now asserts ROUTABILITY (find_handler, the same route
    resolution pveproxy uses), not just registration — the old check passed
    while the endpoint was unreachable.
  * Requires the migration controller / pvecsictl from the matching plugin
    release: the client now posts to the new URL.

 -- CrunchyMonkies <opensource@crunchymonkies.invalid>  Wed, 22 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

pve-csi-copy (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of the token-authorised copy-volume endpoint for the
    proxmox-csi-plugin migration controller. Ships the self-contained Perl
    module tree, the pvedaemon/pveproxy loader drop-ins (managed by the
    maintainer scripts), and /usr/sbin/pve-csi-copy-verify.

